From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:07:54 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add htslib/htscodecs LICENSE files at project root

cyvcf2 statically links htslib (and its bundled htscodecs submodule) into
the cyvcf2 extension by default on Linux (CYVCF2_HTSLIB_MODE=BUILTIN in
CMakeLists.txt), but pyproject.toml sets no [project] license-files list.
scikit-build-core's PEP 639 default license_files glob only covers
LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS* at the project root, so neither
htslib's MIT/Expat-and-BSD LICENSE nor htscodecs' BSD LICENSE.md land in
dist-info/licenses/ even though their code ships in every wheel.

Copy each at the root as LICENSE.htslib and LICENSE.htscodecs, which the
existing default glob already matches with no pyproject.toml change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against brentp/cyvcf2]
---
 LICENSE.htscodecs | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 LICENSE.htslib    | 69 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 114 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.htscodecs
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.htslib

